Shutting down a project stops all billing and resource usage. This action immediately moves the project into a 30-day recovery period
You can recover most resources if you restore a project within the 30-day period. Some services such as Cloud Storage or Pub/Sub might delete data sooner than 30 days. For example, Cloud Storage resources that are protected by soft delete might be deleted after 7 days, depending on the soft delete retention duration, but buckets that have soft delete disabled might be deleted immediately and might not be recoverable.
It can take up to 36 hours for all services within a restored project to become fully functional. In particular, OAuth clients may take 1 to 3 days to be fully operational after a project is restored. If your resources aren't restored after this period, reach out to Google support.
Some services might need to be restarted manually.
gcloud projects describe PROJECT_ID
